 path to an upset.", "watch": "A strong Democratic wave reaching into the Charlotte suburbs, or a late surge of outside spending for Womack, could pull the margin into single digits.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tim Moore (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Tim Moore enters the fall as a clear favorite in this Republican-leaning district anchored by Charlotte's northern suburbs and surrounding exurban counties. He has raised $1.5 million and holds $1.6 million on hand, while Democrat Lakesha Womack has raised under $25,000 and ended the last reporting period in the red. Every major race rating places the seat in Republican territory, and prediction markets give Womack roughly a one-in-seven chance of an upset.\n\nThe main counterweight is the national environment, which favors Democrats in this midterm and could narrow the gap in the Mecklenburg County portion of the district. The only public poll, a Republican-sponsored survey from March, showed Moore ahead by eight points among likely voters. Moore remains on track to win comfortably, with the exact margin hinging on turnout and how far the Democratic environment reaches into this seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0644, "margin": -9.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0543, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0528, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0536, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0567, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0477, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0569, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0517, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.061, "margin": -10.5}]}